From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] linux: read any non-zero online value as online

The kernel documents 2 as a valid value of the online attribute of a power
supply, "Online Programmable", in Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-class-power.
The USB Type-C port manager reports it while a USB PD PPS source is in use.

up_device_supply_refresh_line_power() puts the value as it is into a boolean
property. GLib refuses it with a critical, stores nothing, and still emits
notify. The stored value stays what it was, so this happens again on every
uevent of the supply. Each notify makes the daemon refresh the batteries with
UP_REFRESH_LINE_POWER, which discards the rate for 10 seconds. A battery that
charges from such a supply then reports 0 W and no time to full for as long as
the supply stays programmable.

Seen on a Lenovo TB375FC charging through a charge pump from a PPS charger:
energy-rate 0 W on every update while the port read online 2, and 11.7 W with
26.8 minutes to full right after it went back to 1.

The new test fails without the change: the daemon aborts under
G_DEBUG=fatal-warnings, and without that EnergyRate reads 0 instead of 9.444.
---
--- a/src/linux/up-device-supply.c
+++ b/src/linux/up-device-supply.c
@@ -64,7 +64,9 @@
 	g_object_get (device,
 		      "online", &online_old,
 		      NULL);
-	online_new = g_udev_device_get_sysfs_attr_as_int_uncached (native, "online");
+	/* Anything but 0 is online: a USB PD PPS supply reports 2, "Online
+	 * Programmable", which a boolean property does not take. */
+	online_new = g_udev_device_get_sysfs_attr_as_int_uncached (native, "online") != 0;
 	/* Avoid notification if the value did not change. */
 	if (online_old != online_new)
 		g_object_set (device,
--- a/src/linux/integration-test.py
+++ b/src/linux/integration-test.py
@@ -477,6 +477,61 @@
         )
         self.stop_daemon()
 
+    def test_props_online_programmable_ac(self):
+        """line power reporting Online Programmable, as a USB PD PPS supply does"""
+
+        ac = self.testbed.add_device(
+            "power_supply",
+            "AC",
+            None,
+            ["type", "USB", "usb_type", "C PD [PD_PPS]", "online", "1"],
+            [],
+        )
+        self.testbed.add_device(
+            "power_supply",
+            "BAT0",
+            None,
+            [
+                "type",
+                "Battery",
+                "present",
+                "1",
+                "status",
+                "Charging",
+                "charge_full",
+                "10500000",
+                "charge_full_design",
+                "11000000",
+                "charge_now",
+                "7875000",
+                "current_now",
+                "787000",
+                "voltage_now",
+                "12000000",
+            ],
+            [],
+        )
+
+        self.start_daemon()
+        devs = self.proxy.EnumerateDevices()
+        self.assertEqual(len(devs), 2)
+        ac_up = next(d for d in devs if "line_power_AC" in d)
+        bat0_up = next(d for d in devs if "battery_BAT0" in d)
+        self.assertAlmostEqual(self.get_dbus_dev_property(bat0_up, "EnergyRate"), 9.444)
+
+        # The supply stays the same, so the rate must stay trusted
+        self.testbed.set_attribute(ac, "online", "2")
+        self.testbed.uevent(ac, "change")
+        time.sleep(1)
+        self.testbed.uevent(ac, "change")
+        time.sleep(1)
+
+        self.assertEqual(self.daemon.poll(), None, "daemon crashed")
+        self.assertEqual(self.get_dbus_dev_property(ac_up, "Online"), True)
+        self.assertEqual(self.get_dbus_property("OnBattery"), False)
+        self.assertAlmostEqual(self.get_dbus_dev_property(bat0_up, "EnergyRate"), 9.444)
+        self.stop_daemon()
+
     def test_props_online_ac(self):
         """properties with online AC"""
 
